<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Sept - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world cargo airport in Jan-Sept - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-September 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in January-September 1996, with the volume they handled, the percentage change over January-September 1995 and their January-September 1995 ranking, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  (1) Memphis		1,401,345 tonnes  up    0.2pct</p>
<p> 2  (2) Los Angeles	  1,251,007 tonnes  up    8.4</p>
<p> 3  (3) Miami		  1,239 373 tonnes  up    8.0</p>
<p> 4  (4) New York	     1,190,204 tonnes  up    1.4</p>
<p> 5  (5) Tokyo		  1,172,637 tonnes  down  4.9</p>
<p> 6  (6) Hong Kong	    1,126,671 tonnes  up    5.0</p>
<p> 7  (7) Frankfurt	    1,092,334 tonnes  up    2.1</p>
<p> 8  (8) Louisville	   1,018,699 tonnes  up    1.5</p>
<p> 9  (9) Seoul		    973,415 tonnes  up    9.9</p>
<p> 10(10) Anchorage		936,968 tonnes  up   31.1</p>
<p> 11(11) Chicago		  908,069 tonnes  down  0.2</p>
<p> 12(12) Singapore		876,229 tonnes  up    5.8</p>
<p> 13(13) London Heathrow	838,598 tonnes  up    1.2</p>
<p> 14(14) Amsterdam		810,868 tonnes  up   10.6</p>
<p> 15(15) Paris-CDG		716,239 tonnes  up    3.7</p>
<p> 16(16) New York Newark	705,721 tonnes  up    0.4</p>
<p> 17(17) Atlanta		  685,703 tonnes  up    1.9</p>
<p> 18(19) Taipei		   565,141 tonnes  up    0.1</p>
<p> 19(18) Dallas-Fort Worth    563,182 tonnes  up    0.1</p>
<p> 20(20) Dayton		   533,961 tonnes  up   16.2</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
